311 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E (KODAK IS AN AMERICAN FILM COMPANY FOUNDED IN 1880 IT STANDS AS A PIONEER OF CONSUMER PHOTOGRAPHY. SPECIALIZING IN COMMERCIAL PRINT AND ADVANCED MATERIALS & CHEMICALS NOW KODAK HAS STOOD THE TEST OF TIME FROM EARLY FILM CAMERAS TO INVENTING THE FIRST DIGITAL CAMERA. TODAY KODAK IS FAR SMALLER THAN AT ITS PEAK BUT CONTINUES TO OPERATE AS A GLOBAL TECHNOLOGY COMPANY. ITS CORE BUSINESSES INCLUDE COMMERCIAL PRINTING SYSTEMS FOR PACKAGING AND PUBLISHING, ADVANCED MATERIALS AND SPECIALTY CHEMICALS USED IN ELECTRONICS AND INDUSTRIAL MANUFACTURING, AND A MOTION-PICTURE FILM DIVISION THAT STILL SUPPLIES MAJOR HOLLYWOOD STUDIOS. KODAK ALSO EARNS REVENUE BY LICENSING ITS WELL-KNOWN BRAND FOR CONSUMER PRODUCTS. HEADQUARTERS ARE IN ROCHESTER, NEW YORK, AND THE COMPANY EMPLOYS A FEW THOUSAND PEOPLE WORLDWIDE, GENERATING ABOUT $1 BILLION IN ANNUAL REVENUE.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
312 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
313 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 255 0 R
/E (TODAY KODAK FACES THE CHALLENGE OF STAYING RELEVANT IN A WORLD DOMINATED BY DIGITAL IMAGING, BUT IT RETAINS VALUABLE STRENGTHS: A FAMOUS BRAND, DEEP EXPERTISE IN IMAGING SCIENCE AND MATERIALS, AND A LOYAL PROFESSIONAL FILM MARKET. THESE ASSETS GIVE THE COMPANY OPPORTUNITIES TO REPOSITION ITSELF IN COMMERCIAL PRINTING, ADVANCED MATERIALS, AND SPECIALTY IMAGING AS IT SEEKS LONG-TERM STABILITY.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
